  "name": "porpoise",
  "_about": "THE HARBOUR PORPOISE (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/bigmam/porpoise.py, built from scratch on the dolphin's plan): 1.6 m, STOCKY and rounded, a small round head with NO BEAK (the forehead sloping evenly to a blunt snout, a small short mouth), a low TRIANGULAR dorsal fin just behind the middle (straight leading edge, the trailing edge nearly upright), small rounded dark flippers set well forward, 0.45 m flukes; dark grey back fading to paler flanks and a white belly, a dark line from the mouth's corner to the flipper. A swimmer (`fly`): its tail pitches on four bones a beat apart. Written whole by its script.",
